  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 226 PM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nOn Sunday, temperatures will be in the upper 70s to low 80s with\nwinds lessening as the surface low pressure system moves off\ntoward the Great Lakes. Going into Monday, the upper level flow\nwill once again turn zonal as the remnants of tropical cyclone\nIsaias pushes off into the Atlantic. \n\nThere will be slight chances for light precipitation on Monday\nin the far northern counties as a shortwave moves across\nManitoba/Ontario; however, being so far disconnected from the\ngreatest lift has led precipitation chances to be less than \n20%. Temperatures on Tuesday and Wednesday should be pleasant \nand fall-like with highs in the mid 60s to low 70s before \nsouthwesterly flow aloft returns mid-week and a large trough \ndigs over the western US. Effects from this trough are uncertain\nat this time due to model differences, but will be something to\nmonitor over the weekend into next week.",
